olling uncertainty inflated.", "Incumbent Russ Fulcher (R) is running."]}, "overview": "Republican incumbent Russ Fulcher is seeking another term in a district that has voted roughly 22 points more Republican than the country. Fundraising strongly favors him: he has raised about $663,000 with $245,000 on hand, while Democrat Kaylee Peterson has raised about $181,000 with under $15,000 available. Independent Sarah Zabel and Constitution Party candidate Brendan Gomez also appear on the ballot.\n\nThe available polls, all fielded in July, show Fulcher ahead by margins ranging from roughly five to twenty-one points, though the newest survey is now two months old and samples are modest. Prediction markets give Fulcher about a 95 percent chance of holding the seat, and no expert rating outlets list the race as competitive. Money, fundamentals, and polling all point to a comfortable Republican hold, with Peterson needing an unusual late shift to close a double-digit gap.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.0149, "margin": -16.84}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.0123, "margin": -18.0}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.0169, "margin": -17.5}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.0127, "margin": -18.0}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.0192, "margin": -16.0}, {"date": "2026-09-27", "p_dem": 0.006, "margin": -19.0}, {"date": "2026-09-28", "p_dem": 0.0083, "margin": -18.0}, {"date": "2026-09-29", "p_dem": 0.0149, "margin": -18.0}, {"date": "2026-09-30", "p_dem": 0.0221, "margin": -17.5}, {"date": "2026-10-01", "p_dem": 0.0086, "margin": -18.0}, {"date": "2026-10-02", "p_dem": 0.0165, "margin": -18.0}, {"date": "2026-10-03", "p_dem": 0.0146, "margin": -18.0}, {"date": "2026-10-04", "p_dem": 0.0228, "margin": -16.0}, {"date": "2026-10-05", "p_dem": 0.011, "margin": -18.0}, {"date": "2026-10-06", "p_dem": 0.019, "margin": -17.5}]}